                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0e221777-fb69-33b5-9235-70d671088dd4",
                                        "entry_id": "7dcd9b93-439b-3e04-b7a8-0c06bfe312f8",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to introduce an explanation or clarification: in other words, i.e."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "informal",
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "29d80cd8-dc78-4ed3-bbcd-c26570a678bd",
                                                "sense_id": "0e221777-fb69-33b5-9235-70d671088dd4",
                                                "text": "“The player should usually be able to play more quickly than that and is encouraged to do so,” the guidelines state, with golfers that exceed 40 seconds – AKA “bad time” – “informed as soon as practicable” by a tournament official."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "35163938-2302-4b0d-a3ad-e93d724c6055",
                                                "sense_id": "0e221777-fb69-33b5-9235-70d671088dd4",
                                                "text": "“This color is golden blonde in color and tone, with ‘10k gold lights’ that have a cool reflect for the perfect sparkle,” says celebrity hairstylist Matt Rez, who claims this will be the biggest hair color trend this fall (aka take notes)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6a0b7e41-b176-4177-911c-323e1156999f",
                        "source_entry_id": "601b4465-e3b2-34dc-bd0f-db0e5bc4665c",
                        "source_sense_id": "a96400fc-78c5-355f-b26d-17755e3aba25",
                        "target_lang_word": "alias",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "alias",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "021d7a68-0d6f-374e-a42d-bc95151ce49f",
                                        "entry_id": "afa70b19-db41-392a-b8ac-496e66f6bfd5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Otherwise; at another time; in other circumstances; otherwise called; also known as; formerly known as."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25e0ee7b-37c3-4371-9fc8-59f371003009",
                                                "sense_id": "021d7a68-0d6f-374e-a42d-bc95151ce49f",
                                                "text": "Hitherto the commanding influence of Sir Robert Evelyn's character had sunk his own into insignificance—now he had no \"rival near the throne,\" alias the bench of county magistrates."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5f6ee7f-faca-472b-9c1d-d4f6825dce3b",
                                                "sense_id": "021d7a68-0d6f-374e-a42d-bc95151ce49f",
                                                "text": "When indeed a Popish monarch may fill our throne, and the successor of St. Peter shall be the spiritual head of our Church; then shall your “esoterics,” alias “Church principles,” be in the ascendant in our Universities, and Who shall say that we may not have a Thorp lecturer in each of our Colleges, Neale and Webb scholarships, Regii professores supplying the places of those who shall now be superannuated, all teaching, and empowered to confer degrees in the, symbolism of mystical divinity:—the professor of music, not dealing as he now must, with crotchets and quavers, but in the far higher branches of the sacramentality of sounds, with their correspondent colours, instruments, bearing, &c. &c., and so of others?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "619eb606-ec89-30eb-b68a-9fbe5b30ecd9",
                                        "entry_id": "afa70b19-db41-392a-b8ac-496e66f6bfd5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Used to connect the different names of a person who has gone by two or more, and whose true name is for any cause doubtful"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "123c99e3-609f-49a9-a36b-dc7ff6b01dda",
                                                "sense_id": "619eb606-ec89-30eb-b68a-9fbe5b30ecd9",
                                                "text": "Smith, alias Simpson."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
